rs between a player and referee", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[118, 118]], "note": "caveat that bias occurrence by game context cannot be assessed"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[119, 119]], "assertion": "dyads with only one game dominate the sample, with a median of 1 game", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dyads", "games"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[120, 120]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[121, 121]], "note": "list item label: Multiple comparisons"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[122, 122]], "assertion": "no adjustment was made for testing multiple specifications", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple comparisons", "model specifications"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[123, 123]], "note": "caveat that closeness of p-value to 0.05 raises multiple-testing concerns"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[124, 124]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[125, 125]], "note": "subheading: Possible Sources of Bias"}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[126, 126]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[127, 127]], "assertion": "dark-skinned players are more likely to play forward (23% vs 13%) and less likely to be goalkeeper (2% vs 12%) than light-skinned players, a position imbalance that may leave residual confounding by play style even after adjusting for position", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position", "dark-skinned players"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[128, 128]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[129, 129]], "note": "intro noting lack of information about game-context factors"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[130, 133]], "assertion": "the analysis lacks data on score differential when cards were issued, game importance, home/away status, and team quality or reputation", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["score differential", "game importance", "home/away status", "team quality"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[134, 134]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[135, 135]], "assertion": "non-random pairing of referees and players could bias estimates if certain referees systematically officiate more or fewer dark-skinned players and also have different card-issuing tendencies", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["referees", "players", "selection into dyads"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[136, 136]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[137, 137]], "assertion": "measurement error in height, weight, and age could lead to residual confounding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["height", "weight", "age"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[138, 138]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[139, 139]], "note": "subheading: Key Assumptions and Whether They Were Met"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[141, 141]], "note": "list item label: No unmeasured confounding"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "the no-unmeasured-confounding assumption is judged partially met", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["no unmeasured confounding assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [140, 141]}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "the analysis adjusted for major observable confounders: position, league, anthropometrics, age, and exposure", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position", "league", "anthropometrics", "age", "exposure"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [139, 141]}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "play style, game context, and other factors were not adjusted for, leaving a moderate residual confounding concern", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["play style", "game context"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [139, 140]}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[143, 143]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "list item label: Positivity (overlap)"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[145, 145]], "assertion": "the positivity assumption is judged met: both dark and light-skinned players are observed across covariate levels, with no complete separation, though distributions differ", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["positivity assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[147, 147]], "note": "list item label: Correct model specification"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "the correct-model-specification assumption is judged likely met", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model specification assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [148, 149, 150]}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "logistic regression was used as appropriate for the binary outcome and key confounders were included", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["logistic regression", "confounders"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [147, 149, 150]}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "linearity assumptions for continuous covariates may not be perfectly met, though this is judged unlikely to substantially bias the main estimate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous covariates", "linearity assumption"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [147, 148, 150]}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses with different skin tone operationalizations support the robustness of the finding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses", "skin tone"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [147, 148, 149]}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[149, 149]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[150, 150]], "note": "list item label: Independence"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "the independence assumption is judged partially met", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [154, 155, 156, 157]}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "the analysis accounted for clustering by player (multiple dyads per player)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering", "player"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [153, 155, 156, 157]}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "the analysis did not account for clustering by referee", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["clustering", "referee"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [153, 154, 156, 157]}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "not clustering by referee could lead to underestimated standard errors if referee-level heterogeneity is substantial", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors", "referee heterogeneity"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [153, 154, 155, 157]}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses suggest the effect is robust to this lack of referee clustering", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [153, 154, 155, 156]}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[153, 153]], "note": "list item label: Measurement validity"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "the measurement validity assumption is judged reasonably met", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["measurement validity assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [161, 162]}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "skin tone ratings show high inter-rater reliability (r=0.92, 76.8% perfect agreement)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone ratings", "inter-rater reliability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [160, 162]}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "skin tone from photos may not perfectly reflect real-world perception", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [160, 161]}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[155, 155]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "list item label: Missing completely at random (MCAR)"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "the MCAR assumption is judged uncertain; photos were available for 86% of dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["MCAR assumption", "dyads"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [166, 167]}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "if photo availability correlates with player prominence, league, or other factors affecting red card risk, this could introduce selection bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["photo availability", "selection bias"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [165, 167]}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "the MCAR assumption cannot be tested with the available data", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["MCAR assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [165, 166]}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[158, 158]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[159, 159]], "note": "subheading: Sensitivity to Assumptions"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "intro sentence: the finding is moderately robust"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[162, 162]], "assertion": "a median split specification gives RD=0.17pp (p=0.049), an attenuated but still significant effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["median split specification", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "a continuous skin tone specification gives OR=1.29 per unit (p=0.028), a stronger and more significant effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone specification", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 164]], "assertion": "results are consistent in direction and statistical significance across specifications, though magnitudes vary", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model specifications"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[165, 165]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "caveat that p-values near 0.05 across specifications put the finding on the border of conventional significance"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[167, 170]], "note": "caveat listing possible sensitivities: unmeasured confounders, skin tone categorizations, model specifications, multiple-comparison corrections"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[171, 171]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[173, 173]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "section heading: Additional Context"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[176, 176]], "note": "subheading: Covariate Balance"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[177, 177]], "note": "intro sentence: the two groups differ on several dimensions"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[178, 178]], "assertion": "dark-skinned players are much more likely to be forwards (23% vs 13%) and much less likely to be goalkeepers (2% vs 12%)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position", "dark-skinned players", "light-skinned players"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 186, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 179]], "assertion": "dark-skinned players are more represented in England (38% vs 24%) and France (30% vs 11%), and less in Germany (19% vs 37%)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league", "dark-skinned players"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 187, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "there are minimal differences between groups in age, height, and weight", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["age", "height", "weight"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "the number of games per dyad is similar between groups (3.0 vs 3.1)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["games per dyad"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[183, 183]], "assertion": "the covariate differences between groups underscore the importance of covariate adjustment and suggest unadjusted comparisons would be misleading", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["covariate adjustment"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[184, 184]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "subheading: Unadjusted vs Adjusted Estimates"}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[186, 186]], "assertion": "the unadjusted risk difference is 0.18pp (dark 1.41% vs light 1.23%)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["unadjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 194, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference is 0.23pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "adjustment slightly increased the risk-difference estimate, suggesting negative confounding, i.e. dark-skinned players might have characteristics that would reduce red card risk absent discrimination", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference", "confounding"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[191, 191]], "note": "subheading: Clinical/Practical Significance"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "intro sentence: practical importance is debatable"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "a 0.23pp increased risk translates to an extra 2-3 red cards per 1,000 dyads, small but non-trivial given the severity of red card consequences", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference", "red cards"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 201, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[194, 194]], "assertion": "aggregated across thousands of players and games, the effect could amount to systematic disadvantage", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dark-skinned players"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 202, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "situates finding within broader implicit-bias-in-officiating literature"}, {"id": 203, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 204, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "section heading: Reproducibility"}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "the analyses are fully reproducible from the provided Python script (final_analysis.py) and dataset (./data/soccer/soccer.csv)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["Python script", "dataset"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 209, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 205]], "assertion": "the script includes complete data loading and preprocessing, all variable transformations, primary and sensitivity analyses, and generation of all reported statistics and visualizations", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["script"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[207, 207]], "assertion": "the software used includes Python 3.11, pandas 2.0.3, statsmodels 0.14.0, numpy 1.24.3, matplotlib 3.7.1, and seaborn 0.12.2", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 212, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[208, 208]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 213, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[209, 209]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 214, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[210, 210]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[211, 211]], "note": "section heading: Conclusion (final)"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[213, 213]], "assertion": "the data provide statistically significant evidence that dark-skinned players receive more red cards than light-skinned players, even after accounting for position, league, anthropometrics, age, and exposure", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dark-skinned players", "red cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [218]}, {"id": 218, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[213, 213]], "assertion": "the effect size is small, the confidence interval barely excludes zero, several limitations temper confidence in a causal interpretation, the finding is consistent with implicit or explicit bias but cannot rule out unmeasured confounding, and further research on play style, game context, and referee characteristics would strengthen causal inference", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval", "causal interpretation"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [217]}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[214, 214]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[215, 215]], "assertion": "the final verdict is SUPPORTED, with the caveats that the effect is small, the evidence is not overwhelmingly strong (p=0.042), and alternative explanations cannot be definitively ruled out", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}]}}